---
code: lint-file-count-drift
when-fires: the lintable-file count disagrees with --expect-files. cli/main.rs lint_command. {expected} is the declared count, {found} what the invocation saw.
why: 27R section 8b: the count is a scope assertion, so drift means the glob silently stopped covering what CI thought it covered - clean-because-empty is the failure it catches.
---
-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=webhost.sh
error[lint-file-count-drift]: `--expect-files` declared 12 lintable files, but
Dorc saw 9; the lint's scope has drifted.

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: lint-file-count-drift
{{expected}} = "12"
{{found}} = "9"
